        ("Are Hamersley's 1970s homes at high risk of termites?", "Yes. Timber roof framing, fences and pergolas from 1968 to 1981 have had half a century on warm Karrakatta sand over limestone, and most were built without a termite management system. Garden beds and paving have crept over the weep holes on many. A yearly inspection to AS 4349.3 is the minimum. <a href=\"/termite-inspection-perth\">Book a termite inspection</a>."),
        ("Why are ants so persistent in Hamersley?", "Coastal brown ants thrive in warm, well-drained sand under brick paving, and Hamersley's cul-de-sac layout means colonies link across several backyards. A surface spray splits and spreads them. We use slow-acting non-repellent products and baits, APVMA-registered and applied to label, that the workers carry back so the colony collapses. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
