        ("How quickly can you get to Kallaroo from Warwick?", "About fifteen minutes along Warwick Road, Marmion Avenue and Whitfords Avenue. Same-day for active pests such as a rat in the ceiling or a wasp nest is usually possible, and routine treatments are booked within the week."),
        ("Are the 1970s homes in Kallaroo at real termite risk?", "Yes, and it is the age of the roof framing and the depth of the limestone that matter most. Timber framing over strip footings gives termites a direct path from the ground, and limestone pockets keep moisture close to the slab. An inspection to AS 4349.3 every twelve months is the standard we recommend for original Whitfords-era homes. <a href=\"/termite-inspection-perth\">Book an inspection</a>."),
        ("Why do the ants in my Kallaroo driveway keep coming back?", "Because a repellent spray only moves a coastal brown ant colony sideways. They live in super-colonies with many queens spread across several blocks, so we use a non-repellent product and bait that the workers carry back to the nest, applied to label, and we treat the paving edges and retaining walls where the colonies actually are. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
        ("Do rats come off the coastal dunes into Kallaroo homes?", "They do, particularly along the Northshore streets closest to the Whitfords Nodes foreshore. Salt air corrodes the galvanised mesh at eaves and vents faster than it does inland, and once a gap opens the rats find it. We bait to label and give you a written proofing list so the problem does not repeat next winter. <a href=\"/rodent-control-perth\">Rodent management</a>."),
