        ("Why are coastal brown ants so hard to shift in Mullaloo?", "Warm, well-drained sand over limestone is exactly what they like, and the retaining walls and paving on the slopes give them endless nesting space. They form linked colonies across several properties, so a repellent spray just moves them next door. We use a slow-acting non-repellent product and bait to label so the colony collapses. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
