        ("My Currambine home is on a slab. Do I still need a termite inspection?", "Yes. Slab-on-ground removes timber from the ground but not the risk: termites come through plumbing and electrical penetrations, shrinkage cracks and any point where paving or garden beds have been built above the slab edge. Many 1990s homes have had their original management zone bridged that way. An inspection to AS 4349.3 every twelve months is the standard. <a href=\"/termite-inspection-perth\">Book an inspection</a>."),
        ("Why are the ants in my Currambine driveway so persistent?", "Because coastal brown ants here live in super-colonies with many queens, linked across neighbouring blocks under paving and retaining walls. A repellent spray only splits the colony and moves it. We treat with a slow-acting non-repellent product and bait to label so the workers carry it back and the colony collapses. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
        ("Do the golf course lakes cause mosquito problems in Currambine?", "On the blocks that back onto the Joondalup golf course, yes, especially on still spring and summer evenings. We treat the shaded vegetation where adult mosquitoes rest, applied to label, and walk your block for the pot saucers, gutters and retic pits that breed them close to the house. <a href=\"/mosquito-control-perth\">Mosquito management</a>."),
        ("What is the investment for a general pest treatment in Currambine?", "A typical three-bedroom home, internal and external, sits in the $250 to $350 range. Every job is quoted itemised in writing. <a href=\"/pest-control-prices-perth\">See the investment guide</a>."),
