    now="Spring in Westminster brings coastal brown ants along driveways and into kitchens, German cockroaches surging in warm units, and rats looking for nesting sites after winter. This is 1960s timber-framed housing, so a termite inspection now, before the November swarm, is the single most valuable job on the calendar.",
