        "The suburb was gazetted in 1940 but stayed bush until the school opened in 1956, and nearly all the original housing dates from 1973 to 1976: double brick and brick veneer on strip footings with timber roof framing under tiles. Along West Coast Drive and the streets behind it many of those homes have been replaced with large two-storey builds on slabs, with cavity walls, steel framing and alfresco areas up against the slab edge. The foreshore is young white Quindalup dune sand; a block or two back it becomes shallow yellow sand over Tamala limestone, which is why the streets climb so steeply from the beach to Braden Park and the Sheppard Way shops.",
