        ("Why are coastal brown ants so bad in Marmion?", "Warm, well-drained sand over limestone is the habitat they were named for. They form linked super-colonies with many queens across several properties. Repellent sprays split the colony; slow-acting non-repellent products and baits collapse it. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
        ("Does salt air change how you treat a Marmion home?", "It changes the proofing. Galvanised mesh and flashings corrode faster near the ocean, so gaps at eaves and roof penetrations open sooner and rodents find them. We recommend stainless or aluminium mesh and check the roofline more carefully than we would inland."),
