        "Koondoola Regional Bushland is 137 hectares of Banksia attenuata woodland with jarrah, sheoak and, on the lower ground, melaleuca and flooded gum over former wetland, listed in 2000 as Bush Forever Site 201. It burnt in 2012 and again in 2021, and each time rats, spiders and native cockroaches pushed hard into the surrounding streets. The old wetland ground on the bushland's low side holds moisture through summer, which is where termite colonies stay active when the rest of the sand is dry. Koondoola Park and Butterworth Reserve add irrigated turf, and the bus routes along Marangaroo Drive, Alexander Drive and Beach Road make it an easy run from Warwick.",
