        ("How serious is termite risk for a 1970s home in Koondoola?", "Serious enough for annual inspection. Timber roof framing, fifty years of extensions and paving, and a 137-hectare woodland with moist former-wetland ground next door all add up. An inspection to AS 4349.3 finds activity and conducive conditions early, when the fix is a management system rather than new roof timbers."),
        ("What is the best way to deal with ants in Koondoola?", "Identify the species first. Coastal brown ants, the usual culprit, live in super-colonies under paving and slab edges and get worse after a repellent spray. We treat with slow-acting non-repellent product and baits applied to label so the whole colony collapses. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
        ("Do rats come from Koondoola Regional Bushland?", "Yes, especially after the bush dries in late spring and after fires like 2012 and 2021. Streets backing the reserve get the most roof activity. External baiting to label, proofing of eaves, valleys and weep holes, and a roof-void check keep them out. <a href=\"/rodent-control-perth\">Rodent management</a>."),
