        "North Beach was a holiday spot before it was a suburb. Fishing shacks and weekenders went up around Flora Terrace and Castle Street in the 1940s and 1950s, the postal district was approved in 1954 and by the early 1960s most of the streets were built. What is left is a genuine mix: pre-war and post-war timber-framed cottages, 1960s and 1970s brick-and-tile on big 900 square metre lots, and a steady run of modern two-storey homes replacing them near the ocean. The ground is Quindalup dune sand on the foreshore and shallow yellow sand over Tamala limestone up the slope towards Marmion Avenue. Old timber framing on limestone is the combination subterranean termites like most.",
