        ("How quickly can you get to North Beach from Warwick?", "About ten minutes down Beach Road and Marmion Avenue. Same-day for active pests is usually possible, and we group North Beach with Trigg, Watermans Bay and Carine so there is nearly always a technician nearby."),
        ("Are the older North Beach homes at higher termite risk?", "Yes. The 1940s to 1960s houses have timber floors, timber roof framing and often no original termite management system. Sitting on shallow limestone next to a wetland reserve adds moisture and shelter. An inspection to AS 4349.3 every twelve months is the right interval for that housing, with a management system to AS 3660.2 if activity or conducive conditions are found."),
        ("Why do I get so many ants in North Beach?", "Coastal brown ants. They form linked super-colonies with many queens under paving, limestone retaining walls and driveway edges, and a repellent spray only splits them into more colonies. We use slow-acting non-repellent products and baits, APVMA-registered and applied to label, so the colony collapses. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
