    now="Spring in Alexander Heights is ant season first: coastal brown ant trails appear along paving edges and under bins as the ground warms, then redbacks re-establish in retic boxes and under outdoor furniture. Roof rats are still active from winter. With most homes now around forty years old, a termite inspection before the November swarm season is the single most useful spring job here.",
