    now="Spring in Innaloo: the ground is still wet from winter, so American cockroaches are coming up out of the stormwater lines on the lower streets and coastal brown ants are trailing along the warming paving. German cockroaches in units never stopped. For the timber-framed cottages, a termite inspection now, while the subfloor is still damp, catches activity well before the November flights.",
