        "Until the late 1990s Pearsall was simply the southern end of Wanneroo, market gardens and paddocks on the Spearwood dune system. It was cut out as its own suburb and built up quickly, so almost every home along Willespie Drive and the streets around Covent, Salitage and Voyager Parks is slab-on-ground brick and tile from the last twenty-five years or so, with the odd two-storey rebuild. Slab construction keeps timber off the ground, but termites do not need to reach the frame from below; they come up through slab penetrations, expansion joints and the gap behind a garden bed that has been built up against the brickwork. Pearsall's free-draining yellow sand also suits coastal brown ants, which have moved in under paving and driveways across the suburb.",
