        "Tuart Hill grew slowly after the road to Wanneroo went through in 1872, then filled in quickly after the Second World War and was complete by the 1960s. The housing runs from post-war austerity cottages, a good number of them still timber-framed, through 1950s and 1960s brick and tile, 1960s flats and now two-storey rebuilds and higher-density development around the Main Street district centre. The ground is Spearwood dune sand, yellow and free-draining, with the low, damp ground toward Dog Swamp on the Yokine side. Old timber framing, hardwood floors and seventy-year-old drainage mean termites, rodents and cockroaches all have somewhere to go in a Tuart Hill home.",
