    now="September around Jackadder Lake means the first mosquito evenings of the season and coastal brown ants surfacing on the paving as the sand warms. Rats that wintered in the roof are still there and want clearing before they breed. With most of Woodlands built in the 1960s on timber roof framing, a termite inspection now, ahead of the November alate flights, is well worth doing.",
