        "Beldon sits about three kilometres back from the beach between Marmion Avenue and the Mitchell Freeway, with Ocean Reef Road along its northern side. The name was approved in 1975 and the first house packages were marketed in 1977, so the housing is remarkably consistent: single-storey double brick and brick veneer with tiled roofs on timber framing, on generous blocks laid out along Craigie Drive and Gradient Way. The ground is Spearwood dune system, yellow sand over Tamala limestone, which drains fast on top but holds moisture in limestone pockets below. That is the combination subterranean termites use in a dry Perth summer, and forty-year-old timber roof framing with original garden beds against the walls gives them the timber to work on.",
