    now="Spring in Coolbinia brings ants up through old brick paving and along kitchen skirtings, and spiders back onto the brickwork after winter. Rats that wintered in roof voids are heading out to the reserve and garden sheds to nest, which is the time to seal the entry points. With almost the whole suburb built before 1960 on timber framing, a termite inspection to AS 4349.3 now, before the November alate flights, is the most valuable booking of the year.",
