        "Ashby was carved out of Wanneroo in 1997 and built up through the 2000s, so almost every home is slab-on-ground double brick with a tiled or Colorbond roof, steel or treated-pine framing and a small block with paving right up to the walls. Only about 40 per cent of the suburb is developed; the rest is bush and rural lots along Carosa Road and Conti Road that are being subdivided one stage at a time. The ground east of Wanneroo Road is the grey Bassendean sand of the Gnangara mound: deep, free-draining and sitting over a large groundwater body. Termites live comfortably in it, and the old banksia and jarrah stands that remain are full of established colonies.",
