    now="Spring in Kiara starts with ants on the paving and spiders back in the sheds and pergolas, then mosquitoes off the Bennett Brook wetlands by late September as the water table is at its highest. Roof rats are breeding now. With the original homes past fifty years on timber framing, a termite inspection to AS 4349.3 before the November alate flights is the most important job of the season.",
