        ("Are Kiara's 1970s homes a termite risk?", "Yes. Fifty-year-old timber roof framing, fascias and pergolas, sheds and garden beds against the walls, and Bassendean sand with a shallow water table is a high-risk combination. We inspect the roof void and footings to AS 4349.3 and install management systems to AS 3660.2. <a href=\"/termite-inspection-perth\">Book an inspection</a>."),
        ("Why do the ants in Kiara keep coming back?", "Because the colony is under the paving, the shed slab and the neighbours' yard as one linked nest, and a repellent spray only splits it. We use APVMA-registered non-repellent products and baits applied to label so the whole colony collapses. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Read more</a>."),
        ("Where do the rats in my Kiara roof come from?", "The reserves and greenways on three sides of the suburb, plus old sheds, fruit trees and the eave gaps common on 1970s roofs. We bait to label and give you a written list of the entry points to seal so it does not repeat next winter. <a href=\"/rodent-control-perth\">Rodent management</a>."),
        ("What is the investment for a general pest treatment in Kiara?", "A typical three-bedroom home, internal and external, sits in the $250 to $350 range. Every job is quoted itemised in writing. <a href=\"/pest-control-prices-perth\">See the investment guide</a>."),
